  "unreadable": [],
  "uncertain": [
    "Debug UART: only TX has a leader line to a physical pad (the rightmost). GND is matched to the left square pad by its square symbol, and RX to the middle pad by elimination.",
    "Start end: no connector in the image is labeled USB, so the top/left rule was used. If one of the unlabeled bottom-edge connectors is USB, the 26-pin and 13-pin headers would start at the bottom."
  ],
  "notes": "Image labels Orange Pi ZERO 3 v1.2. The 26-pin diagram reproduces the 2x13 hole grid, with a square marker on the top-left pad, matching the square pad on the board. Right-header pins have no GPIO name. The outermost printed text (RX, OUT, LR, DP...) is the label, and the group box (IR, TV, LINEOUT, USB3, USB2) is a function. On the 26-pin header, functions are read outward from the pin (group box such as I2C3/SPI1/UART5, then the signal name). The 5V box and IN/OUT label span the top two right-column pins, so both are recorded as 5V."
